<section class="section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">VexaScript CLI</p>
    <h1>Compile, bundle, run, serve, inspect, and format from the terminal</h1>
    <p class="lead">The <code>vexa</code> CLI covers building, bundling, serving browser demos with live reload, running, providing syntax definitions in different formats, formatting, testing, exploring the AST, LSP and MCP. Project defaults live in <a href="/config"><code>vexascript.json</code></a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cli-layout">
    <article class="card cli-overview">
      <h3>Core commands</h3>
      <div class="cli-command-list">
        <div>
          <code>build</code> <code class="command_switch">&lt;input.vx|input.ts&gt;</code>
          <p>Compile a VexaScript or TypeScript file to JavaScript, with optional bundling and JSX factory overrides.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>bundle</code> <code class="command_switch">&lt;input&gt;</code>
          <p>Bundle a VexaScript entry file and all referenced modules as ESM output.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>run</code> <code class="command_switch">&lt;input&gt;</code>
          <p>Transpile and execute a VexaScript file with Node.js.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>serve</code> <code class="command_switch">&lt;dir&gt;</code> <code class="command_switch">--bundle &lt;input.vx&gt;</code>
          <p>Serve a static folder on port <code>8080</code> by default, inject the bundle into HTML, and live-reload the page whenever the bundled dependency graph changes.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>test</code> <code class="command_switch">[paths...]</code>
          <p>Discover and run <code>.test.vx</code> files with the built-in inline helpers.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>format</code> <code class="command_switch">&lt;input&gt;</code>
          <p>Format a file in place, optionally writing a copy to a separate output path.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div><code>tokens</code> <code class="command_switch">&lt;input&gt;</code></div>
          <div><code>ast</code> <code class="command_switch">&lt;input&gt;</code></div>
          <p>Inspect the tokenizer output or print a simplified AST for debugging parser behavior.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>syntax</code>
          <span class="command_switch"><code>--monaco</code>, <code>--vscode</code>, <code>--textmate</code>, <code>--codemirror</code></span>
          <p>Export editor grammars</p>
          
          <p>Select editor syntax export targets from the <code>syntax</code> command, or use <code>--target &lt;name&gt;</code> for the explicit target id.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>lsp</code>
          <p>Start the language server. By default using <code class="command_switch">--stdio</code>. This allows editors to get autocompletion and error detection.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>mcp</code>
          <p>Run the MCP navigation server. This enables agents to do accurate operations on VexaScript codebases.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3>Command overview</h3>
      <div class="cli-flag-grid">
        <div>
          <code>-o, --out &lt;file&gt;</code>
          <p>Use the command-specific sections below for the complete flag list.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>--target &lt;mode&gt;</code>
          <p>Use <code>conservative</code> or <code>optimized</code> transpilation modes on build-oriented commands.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>--jsx-factory</code> / <code>--jsx-fragment-factory</code>
          <p>Override JSX emit targets for projects that do not use the default React-style factories.</p>
          <p>It is possible to define those also in the <code>tsconfig.json</code> file.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <code>--root &lt;dir&gt;</code>
          <p>Set the workspace root for the <code>mcp</code> server when resolving files and symbols.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
{% highlightVexaScript %}
vexa build src/main.vx --out dist/main.js --target optimized
vexa serve demo/ --bundle demo/main.vx
vexa syntax --monaco
vexa test samples/
{% endhighlightVexaScript %}
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Command reference</p>
    <h2>Flags and supported forms</h2>
    <p class="lead">These sections mirror <code>vexa help &lt;command&gt;</code>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cli-layout">
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa build &lt;input&gt;</code></h3>
      <p>Compile a file or project to JavaScript.</p>
      <p><code>-o, --out &lt;path&gt;</code> output file or project directory.</p>
      <p><code>--target &lt;mode&gt;</code> <code>conservative</code> or <code>optimized</code>.</p>
      <p><code>--jsx-factory &lt;factory&gt;</code> and <code>--jsx-fragment-factory &lt;factory&gt;</code> override JSX factories.</p>
      <p><code>--bundle</code> bundles the entry and referenced modules; <code>--platform &lt;platform&gt;</code> selects <code>browser</code> or <code>node</code>.</p>
      <p><code>--transpile-only</code> skips semantic diagnostics.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa run &lt;input&gt;</code></h3>
      <p>Transpile and execute a VexaScript file with Node.js.</p>
      <p><code>--target &lt;mode&gt;</code> selects <code>conservative</code> or <code>optimized</code>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa bundle &lt;input&gt;</code></h3>
      <p>Bundle the entry and referenced local and package modules as ESM.</p>
      <p><code>-o, --out &lt;file&gt;</code>, <code>--target &lt;mode&gt;</code>, <code>--jsx-factory &lt;factory&gt;</code>, <code>--jsx-fragment-factory &lt;factory&gt;</code>, and <code>--transpile-only</code>.</p>
      <p><code>--platform &lt;platform&gt;</code> is <code>browser</code> or <code>node</code>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa serve [dir]</code></h3>
      <p>Serve static files, optionally bundle an entry, inject it into HTML, and live-reload on changes.</p>
      <p><code>--bundle &lt;input&gt;</code>, <code>--open</code>, <code>--port &lt;number&gt;</code>, <code>--target &lt;mode&gt;</code>, <code>--jsx-factory &lt;factory&gt;</code>, and <code>--jsx-fragment-factory &lt;factory&gt;</code>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa test [paths...]</code></h3>
      <p>Discover and run <code>.test.vx</code> files. It has no command-specific flags.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa format &lt;input&gt;</code></h3>
      <p>Format a VexaScript file in place.</p>
      <p><code>-w, --write</code> is retained as a deprecated compatibility flag; <code>-o, --out &lt;file&gt;</code> selects another output path.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa tokens &lt;input&gt;</code> and <code>vexa ast &lt;input&gt;</code></h3>
      <p>Print the token stream or simplified AST. Neither command has additional flags.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa syntax</code></h3>
      <p>Print embedded editor syntax definitions.</p>
      <p><code>--target &lt;name&gt;</code>, <code>--monaco</code>, <code>--monaco-language</code>, <code>--monaco-configuration</code>, <code>--vscode</code>, <code>--vscode-grammar</code>, <code>--vscode-configuration</code>, <code>--codemirror</code>, and <code>--textmate</code>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa lsp</code></h3>
      <p>Start the language server. Transport options are passed through to the language-server adapter.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card cli-flags">
      <h3><code>vexa mcp</code></h3>
      <p>Start the MCP codebase-navigation server over JSON-RPC on standard input/output. MCP clients discover these tools through <code>tools/list</code> and invoke them through <code>tools/call</code>.</p>
      <p><code>--root &lt;dir&gt;</code> selects the workspace root used to resolve paths and scan symbols.</p>
      <h4>Provided MCP tools</h4>
      <p><code>vexa_workspace_symbols</code> searches top-level symbols and class members across the workspace. Optional arguments: <code>query</code> (case-insensitive name filter; empty returns all symbols) and <code>root</code>.</p>
      <p><code>vexa_document_symbols</code> lists the symbols declared in one file. Required argument: <code>file</code>.</p>
      <p><code>vexa_hover</code> returns type and documentation information at a position. Required arguments: <code>file</code>, <code>line</code>, <code>character</code>. The line is zero-based and <code>character</code> is a zero-based UTF-16 offset. Optional: <code>root</code>.</p>
      <p><code>vexa_definition</code> navigates to the definition at a position, including imported and cross-file symbols. It accepts the same position arguments as <code>vexa_hover</code>.</p>
      <p><code>vexa_references</code> finds references to the symbol at a position across the workspace. It accepts the same position arguments plus optional <code>includeDeclaration</code>, which defaults to <code>true</code>.</p>
      <p><code>vexa_signature_help</code> returns call-signature help around a position. It accepts the same position arguments as <code>vexa_hover</code>.</p>
      <p><code>vexa_rename</code> builds a cross-file rename edit at a position. Required arguments: <code>file</code>, <code>line</code>, <code>character</code>, and <code>newName</code>. Optional: <code>root</code> and <code>apply</code>; <code>apply</code> defaults to <code>false</code> and writes changes only when set to <code>true</code>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
